{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Flesh to eat.</b> And not to be satisfied — the Torah teaches derech eretz, that one does not eat flesh to satiety. And why did He see fit to bring down bread in the morning and flesh in the evening? Because the bread they asked for properly — for it is impossible for a person without bread — but the flesh they asked for improperly, for they had many cattle, and besides, it was possible for them without flesh. Therefore He gave it to them at a troublesome hour, improperly (Yoma 75a)." "<b>That you murmur against Him.</b> The others who hear you are the ones murmuring."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:39.153352057Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}